	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13370"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148" title="View the profile of Lhyra">Lhyra</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 26<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13370#msg13370"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13370#msg13370">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> December 22, 2004, 02:23:58 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Shhh don&#039;t dispell his rumor.<br /><br />The server is quiet, I like quiet.&nbsp; There are currently fewer assholes on the server.&nbsp; Some guilds did not make it, but it has offered opportunity for us to meet new people.&nbsp; It seems guilds are getting along better then ever before.&nbsp; The people that are left playing Everquest 1, really enjoy the game.&nbsp; There were many people playing that didn&#039;t enjoy it, but for lack of other games out there continued to log on and cause the rest of us grief.&nbsp; For years I have suggested the whiners leave, and by god I think they did....let&#039;s just hope they don&#039;t come back.<br /><br />I hope they don&#039;t condense servers anytime soon, as that may cause a bit of friction for a while.&nbsp; The game supported 400,000 players at one time.&nbsp; I&#039;m sure it has seen it&#039;s max population, but you can bet it&#039;s not going anywhere anytime soon.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13371"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1" title="View the profile of Kinladar">Kinladar</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Ranger Bait<br />
								Administrator<br />
								Veeshan<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/staradmin.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 14456<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13371#msg13371"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13371#msg13371">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> December 22, 2004, 03:03:47 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							With no new players starting the game anymore due to the piss poor idea of naming EQ2 as they did, they have doomed EQ to the fate of EQ.<br /><br />I remember someone posting the logic behind someone at the racks that the local software store, and looking it over, would you buy the &quot;old&quot; EQ, or want to be playing the latest and greatest EQ2?<br /><br />No gamer buys old software. The numbers of new people coming to EQ are done. Stick a fork in it. Server consolidations will only go so far, when people have always been leaving over time etc... but with version 2.0 of the software on the shelves, it&#039;s all over.<br /><br />They shoulda named it anything but EQ2 if they really expected EQ to survive.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.wowrankings.com/viewb.htm?name=Kinladar&amp;s_id=38" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/sig-kinladar-wow.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><a href="http://www.chaoticdiscord.org" target="_blank">Chaotic Discord</a> found in {World of Warcraft}<br />Guild Leader of Fires of Time (Retired)
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg13376"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148" title="View the profile of Lhyra">Lhyra</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 26<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=148"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13376#msg13376"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13376#msg13376">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #7 on:</b> December 22, 2004, 05:31:34 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13371#msg13371">Quote from: Kinladar on December 22, 2004, 03:03:47 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I remember someone posting the logic behind someone at the racks that the local software store, and looking it over, would you buy the &quot;old&quot; EQ, or want to be playing the latest and greatest EQ2?<br /></div><br />I listen to &quot;classic rock&quot;.&nbsp; I think EQ will become the &quot;classic mmorg&quot;.&nbsp; I read reviews before I began playing (velious release), so I&#039;m thinking others would too.&nbsp; EQ2 and WoW are different games from EQ.&nbsp; I don&#039;t think they are better.&nbsp; I think most that quit EQ don&#039;t think the other games are better, but they just had their fill of EQ1 and needed something new.&nbsp; I&#039;m kinda hoping EQ will attract a more mature gamer.&nbsp; The market is saturated with on line games currently.&nbsp; They will all be fighting heavily for the new customer.<br /><br />I can&#039;t imagine they will continue to support forty some servers though.&nbsp; It&#039;s reasonable to expect condensing at some point.&nbsp; It&#039;s only been a couple months.&nbsp; I would guess they would give it six months to a year to watch population.&nbsp; I&#039;m sure many have not cancelled EQ &quot;just in case&quot;, so still pulling in the same revenue.<br /><br />I have met many people from other servers over the years.&nbsp; I know condensing will be stressful, but it&#039;s also kind of exciting thinking about being able to hang out with new people.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
