								<a href="mailto:ktadema@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13383#msg13383"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1343.msg13383#msg13383">Re: You know that EQ ended, right?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> December 22, 2004, 08:34:29 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">&nbsp; The people that are left playing Everquest 1, really enjoy the game.&nbsp; </div><br />Probably a true statement, Lyrha.&nbsp; Probably also a lot of us that really wanted to experience the end game but couldn&#039;t put in enough raid time to meet the stringent raid requirements of the power gamers.&nbsp; Since some power gamers have left, guilds have to lower their standards, allowing people who had the desire, but not the time, to take their vacancies.&nbsp; EQ1 has become a much more casual player friendly game.&nbsp; I like it!!!!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
